  "content": {
    "title": "Otega Oweh drops generational stat line in win over Santa Clara",
    "text": "March 20, 2026, 4:11 p.m. ETThe Kentucky Wildcats, down three with 2.4 seconds to go, somehow beat the Santa Clara Broncos in overtime on Friday afternoon, the first game of the second day of March Madness. The Cats won 89-84, taking down the Broncos in what was a popular upset pick for many. Santa Clara was seen as the best No. 10 seed in the NCAA Tournament, and it certainly played with poise and backed up its much-deserved KenPom rating.However, the Cats had Otega Oweh, and in the end, that's what mattered the most. Oweh went off, as he has been for much of 2026. He dropped 35 points on 11-for-24 shooting to go along with eight rebounds and seven assists. The best part of his entire game was the mere two turnovers he ended with. Oweh drained three triples as well as going 10-for-12 from the free-throw line.That said, per David Cobb, Oweh was the first player with that stat line in an NCAA Tournament game since 1979. No one has done what Oweh did since Hall of Fame forward Larry Bird.The Cats needed all 35 of those points as well, and they got a full effort from Oweh, who played a team-high 43 minutes. Having made that last-second three, Oweh will remember this game for the rest of his life. It has been a dominant run for the 6-foot-5 guard. He put up just 10 points in the Cats' SEC Tournament loss to the Florida Gators, but he has dropped 21, 23, and 28 points in the three games prior. He has stepped up as the Cats' main go-to weapon.Kentucky will move on in the NCAA Tournament and likely take on the No. 2 seed Iowa State Cyclones on Sunday.",
